#pragma code_page(65001)
// res/lang/lo.rc -- Lao, the strings of the interface for `[general] language = "lo"`.
//
// Stage E108, group A: an adaptation of en.rc and ru.rc, not a word-for-word translation. The two
// string tables of this language -- the dialog block and the menu block -- in the order of en.rc.
// Where each string is seen and how much room it has is res/lang/context.tsv; tests/l10n.rs holds
// this file to en.rc. The terms are in l10n/glossary/lo.tsv of the control folder.
//
// ⚠ In an .rc string a backslash is an escape -- one backslash is written as two -- and a double
// quote inside a string is written as two double quotes. The code page line above is this
// file's own: without it rc.exe reads the file in the ANSI code page, silently.

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Lao — `[general] language = "lo"`.
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
